{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Who cause to err.</b> They watch a person's word and cause him to err, in order to punish him, or they cause others to err by their words." "<b>They lay snares.</b> From the root מוקש (Deuteronomy 7:16), and R. Moses the Priest said that they will reprove the reprover, from the root התקוששו וקושו [Zephaniah 2:1], and he said that the shin ought to have had a dagesh."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {1 "The phrase התקוששו וקושו (Zephaniah 2:1) is Ibn Ezra's direct Hebrew quotation of that verse; retained in Hebrew script per discipline."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:54.112803480Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}